{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And redeem her.</b> This teaches that he deducts her redemption payment and she goes out. Rashi explained: that if he acquired her for six years for six maneh and she served two years, she gives four maneh and goes out. And if you ask, what is deducted here — one can say that the years coming are such that she is older and her strength to do work is greater than the years that passed; therefore it is called a deduction."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:36.915888906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}